# D-105 slice 1 (Q39), under --walk-methods: Model and Other agree by name, but their field `x` is a
# reference to InA in one and to InB in the other.  A way through `m\x` would read InB at InA's slots
# -- the correspondence of slice 1 is one level -- so the walked root refuses the admission:
# "an admission to a Structure type through a Structure field of another type".
InA:
    size_t: p 1U
    size_t: q 2U
end: InA
InB:
    size_t: q 20U
    size_t: p 10U
end: InB
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    @: InA x
end: Model
Other:
    @: InB x
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
Other: o
size_t: got 0U
got: rd(o)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
